invariant: INV-48
file: src/mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: the AVX2 copy's ByteDecode12 calls mlkem_poly.c's loop, so a
  session with CH_CPU_AVX2 reads t-hat and s-hat one field at a time.
  Nothing else objects: the loop gives the same coefficients, and only
  the time is wrong. The script requires the copy for x86-64 to call
  mlk_poly_frombytes_avx2 and not mlk_poly_frombytes.

--- old
#ifdef CH_MLKEM_AVX2_COPY
    mlk_poly_frombytes_avx2(p, in);
--- new
#ifdef CH_MLKEM_AVX2_COPY
    mlk_poly_frombytes(p, in);
